# What this repo produces but does not keep. Every entry below corresponds to a
# tool this project actually runs — dune, opam, npm (the VS Code client), python
# (the fitness checks), d2 (the diagrams) — rather than a copied-in catch-all;
# an ignore rule for a tool nobody runs only hides the day someone starts.

# ── OCaml / dune ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# dune keeps everything in _build; the loose artifacts below appear only when a
# compiler is invoked by hand, which is exactly when they are least wanted.
/_build/
*.install
*.merlin
*.annot
*.cmi
*.cmo
*.cmx
*.cmt
*.cmti
*.cma
*.cmxa
*.cmxs
*.o
*.a
*.so
*.byte
*.native
*.exe
# Coverage output, if a run is ever instrumented.
*.coverage
bisect*.coverage
/_coverage/

# ── opam ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A switch created inside the checkout (opam switch create .).
/_opam/
# writ.opam is NOT ignored: it is generated from dune-project by
# (generate_opam_files true), and `opam pin` / `opam install .` must find it in
# the sources before anything is built. Regenerate it with `make build`.

# ── Release output (make release) ────────────────────────────
# The tarball, and the checksum built beside it. Anchored: a `dist/` belonging
# to some future subproject is that subproject's business.
/dist/

# ── Python bytecode ──────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# ── Merge and patch leftovers ────────────────────────────────
# Never intentional, and easy to commit by accident during a conflict.
*.orig
*.rej

# ── Editor / OS cruft ────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~
.idea/
# Personal editor settings. Anchored to the root: nothing here nests one.
/.vscode/

# ── Local tooling and environment state (not project source) ─
# Editor and assistant scratch: how the work gets done on one machine, not part
# of what is built.
.omc/
.afk-flow/
.claude/settings.local.json
.direnv/
.env
